IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgaa-guarantee`

-- Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992, ss 10A, 12, 16B, 17A, 18C, 18D, 19B, 20A, 20C, 32C -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_superannuation-guarantee-administration-act-1992.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Scenario facts used: Chloe c020 (a casual job at fifteen; hours not stated in the scenario, 10 assumed), c032 (an intern at $25
-- an hour), c041 ($70,000 a year, $5,833.33 a month); Jake k041 (a delivery-platform contractor), k060 (a security officer on the
-- award); Daniel d044 (first employees in June 2031). Paydays, pay amounts, holiday lists and the maximum contributions base
-- below are HYPOTHETICAL inputs chosen for the test, not facts from the scenarios or the Act. This edition is the Payday
-- Super text in force from 1 July 2026; the 2018, 2023 and 2024 events are tested only where the provision is unchanged.

`Chloe at fifteen, a casual at the supermarket` MEANS Engagement WITH
    `an employee in the ordinary meaning` IS TRUE
    `works under a contract wholly or principally for their labour` IS FALSE
    `paid as a member of the executive body of a body corporate` IS FALSE
    `a member of a Parliament or a Territory Legislative Assembly` IS FALSE
    `paid to perform or present entertainment, sport or promotion, or for services in connection with it` IS FALSE
    `paid for work on a film, tape, disc or broadcast` IS FALSE
    `holds a public office or is otherwise in government service` IS FALSE
    `a member of a local government council in that capacity` IS FALSE
    `covered by s 12-45(1)(e) of Schedule 1 to the TAA` IS FALSE
    `paid for work wholly or principally domestic or private` IS FALSE
    `hours a week of that work` IS 10

