§ `s 12 -- employee`

#ASSERT `the worker is an employee for the Act` `Chloe at fifteen, a casual at the supermarket`
#ASSERT `the worker is an employee for the Act` `Chloe the intern at $25 an hour`
#ASSERT NOT `the worker is an employee for the Act` `an unpaid placement with no contract for labour`
#ASSERT `the worker is an employee for the Act` `Jake on the platform, contract principally for his labour`
#ASSERT NOT `the worker is an employee for the Act` `Jake on the platform, contract not principally for his labour`
#ASSERT `the worker is an employee for the Act` `Jake at Sentinel on the award`
#ASSERT NOT `the worker is an employee for the Act` `a babysitter for 20 hours a week`
#ASSERT NOT `the worker is an employee for the Act` `a nanny for exactly 30 hours a week`
#ASSERT `the worker is an employee for the Act` `a nanny for 38 hours a week`
#ASSERT NOT `the worker is an employee for the Act` `a local councillor`

